{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115549","id":3221149992,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6__tko","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115549","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115549.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115549.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115549","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115549/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115549/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115549/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/cfa8d762ef8c513faa73b7f08074858475127921","number":115549,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix UPNP code sample using `OK` constant incorrectly","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The returned value is an UPNPResult, not an Error. Both `UPNP.UPNP_RESULT_SUCCESS` and `OK` are equal to 0, so it will behave the same, but it's not identical from a static typing perspective.\r\n\r\n- This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/11671.\r\n\r\nThere is an issue I'm running into when running the code locally: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/11671#issuecomment-3814722181\r\n\r\n```\r\nE 0:00:02:637   node_2d.gd:23 @ _upnp_setup(): /root/Node2D: The caller thread can't call the function `emit_signalp()` on this node. Use `call_deferred()` or `call_deferred_thread_group()` instead.\r\n  <C++ Error>   Condition \"!is_accessible_from_caller_thread()\" is true. Returning: (ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER)\r\n  <C++ Source>  scene/main/node.cpp:4188 @ emit_signalp()\r\n  <Stack Trace> node_2d.gd:23 @ _upnp_setup()\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have the script attached to a Node2D in an empty project. Should we update anything else?\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"","color":"ffddff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","fol